": 954, "session_id": "20261008_104421_77970a", "role": "tool", "content": "{\"success\": true, \"name\": \"spx-momentum-task-execution\", \"file\": \"references/project-conventions.md\", \"content\": \"# trading_data_platform (spx_momentum) conventions\\n\\nRepo root: /home/ttran/code/trading_data_platform. Python 3.12, uv-managed, `src/` layout.\\n\\n## Layout (from the plan; matches disk)\\n```\\nconfig/default.yaml            # yaml baseline for Settings\\nsrc/spx_momentum/\\n  config.py                    # Settings (pydantic-settings, env prefix SPX_)\\n  data/{store,universe,ingest,transform}.py\\n  features/momentum.py\\n  strategy/{base,signal}.py\\n  backtest/{costs,engine,metrics,report}.py\\n  pipeline/tasks.py\\n  ui/dashboard.py\\ntests/                         # test_<module>.py per stage; conftest fixtures\\ndags/momentum_dag.py           # thin Airflow wrapper (Task 14)\\n.superpowers/sdd/<slug>/progress.md   # SDD ledger: setup, rulings, per-task status\\n```\\n\\n## Task map (plan number -> module)\\nT2 config.py · T3 data/store.py · T4 data/universe.py · T5 data/ingest.py ·\\nT6 data/transform.py · T7 features/momentum.py · T8 strategy/ · T9 backtest/costs.py ·\\nT10 backtest/engine.py · T11 backtest/metrics.py · T12 backtest/report.py ·\\nT13 pipeline/tasks.py · T14 dags · T15 ui/dashboard.py.\\n\\n## Config precedence (config.py)\\nkwarg overrides > `SPX_<FIELD>` env (exact case-insensitive match to known fields; unknown\\nSPX_* vars are dropped) > config/default.yaml > pydantic field defaults.\\n`load_settings(path=None, **overrides) -> Settings`; module singleton `settings`.\\nBad values raise a typed pydantic ValidationError, never a crash.\\n\\n## Lake/stage contract (store.py)\\n- `Stage` enum: RAW, CLEAN, FEATURES, POSITIONS, RESULTS -> one dir each under `Settings.data_root`.\\n- `write_upsert(df, stage, key_cols=(\\\"ticker\\\",\\\"date\\\"))` is idempotent: same frame twice => same row count; matching key => replaced, not appended. Datelike `date` coerced to plain date on write.\\n- `read(stage)` returns `pd.DataFrame` (empty frame if stage never written) — call sites must handle empty.\\n- `sql(q)` runs DuckDB; stage names resolve as live views over the stage dir.\\n- parquet writes need a declared pandas engine (pyarrow) — it is a dependency, not optional; an ImportError at read/write means the env lost it, fix the env not the code.\\n\\n## Testing conventions\\n- `tests/conftest.py`: `synthetic_prices` (engineered trends AAA...EEE), `universe_500`, `small_universe`, `lake(tmp_path)` (auto-close), `toy_equity_series`, and an **autouse `_no_network`** guard that fails on any `socket.create_connection`.\\n- External boundaries are patched via module aliases (e.g. `ingest.yf.download`, `universe._fetch_wikipedia_html`), never via sockets.\\n- Stubs for unexecuted tasks are `pytest.skip`-ed functions named after the invariant — when implementing a task, REPLACE them in place keeping the names (they read as the contract).\\n- Gates: `ruff check .` (line-length 100, E/F/I/UP/B) + `mypy src` (strict) + `pytest -q`. Run from repo root with `.venv/bin/...`.\\n\\n## SDD ledger\\n`.superpowers/sdd/2026-10-05-spx-momentum-scaffold/progress.md` — setup notes, env decisions\\n(uv vs pip), interface rulings (e.g. yfinance alias, ticker-regex alnum ruling), and per-task\\n`Task N: complete (commits X..Y, tests: ...)`. Read the task's line for rulings BEFORE\\ndeviating from an ambiguous plan clause — the ledger records the chosen interpretation.\\n\\n## DAG\\nThin DAG imports `spx_momentum.pipeline.tasks` only; retries/backoff live ONLY on the\\ningest node. Makefile `test`/`lint` wrap the gates above.\\n\", \"file_type\": \".md\", \"_source_path\": \"/home/ttran/.hermes/skills/software-development/spx-momentum-task-execution/references/project-conventions.md\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_re625v5k", "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": "skill_view", "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791474367.7229958, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "e4a84abefecc4290882537c1600d8ad9", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": "08728d4a6b8e4836bac9417d58ee38fe"}, {"id": 955, "session_id": "20261008_104421_77970a", "role": "tool", "content": "{\"success\": true, \"name\": \"spx-momentum-task-execution\", \"file\": \"references/fetching-and-pandas3.md\", \"content\": \"# Live-fetch recipes + pandas-3 / ruff break cheat-sheet\\n\\nFor spx_momentum (and any code in this venv: pandas 3.0.6, lxml, duckdb, uv).\\n\\n## Wikipedia constituents (universe.py)\\n- URL: `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_S%26P_500_companies` — SINGULAR.\\nThe plural `Lists_of_S%26P_500_companies` 404s.\\n- MUST send a descriptive `User-Agent` header. urllib's default UA -> Wikipedia 403.\\nThe UA doubles as the contact line per site policy.\\n- The constituents table is the FIRST data table; verify `480 <= len <= 530` after parsing.\\n- `pd.read_html` takes `io.StringIO(html)`, NOT a bare `str` (see pandas-3 below).\\n- Live check (outside pytest):\\n  ```bash\\n  PYTHONPATH=src .venv/bin/python -c \\\"\\n  import spx_momentum.data.universe as u\\n  df = u.fetch_universe('wikipedia'); u.validate_universe(df)\\n  print(len(df), df['ticker'].head().tolist())\\n  \\\"\\n  ```\\n  Expect ~500 rows, e.g. `['MMM','AOS','ABT',...]`. On 4xx, re-check UA and URL\\n  before touching the parser.\\n\\n## yfinance download shapes (ingest.py)\\n- Multi-ticker (`group_by=\\\"ticker\\\"`): DataFrame with MultiIndex columns\\n  `[(ticker, field), ...]`, field in {Open,High,Low,Close,Volume}. Split with\\n  `data.loc[:, ticker]` — the ticker label is at level 0; do not assume `xs(level=1)`.\\n  Drop all-NaN rows with `dropna(how=\\\"all\\\")` (the 2.x `~df.isna(axis=1).all()` idiom\\n  breaks under 3.0, see below).\\n- Single-ticker / flat fallback: plain columns Open/High/Low/Close/Volume with a date index.\\n  In a test double, treat a one-element list call as a single-ticker request, because\\n  \\\"one bad ticker in a batch\\\" must be exercised through BOTH shapes.\\n- Always `auto_adjust=True` (adjusted close lands in `Close`).\\n- For alias-patching keep `import yfinance as yfinance`-style module access at module\\n  scope (`yf: ModuleType = yfinance`); tests patch `ingest.yf.download`. Importing\\n  yfinance is network-free.\\n\\n## pandas 3.0 / lxml / ruff API breaks observed in this venv\\n| 2.x idiom (fails here) | working form |\\n|---|---|\\n| `pd.read_html(html_string)` | `pd.read_html(io.StringIO(html_string))` — with lxml installed a bare str is parsed as a FILE PATH -> FileNotFoundError. |\\n| `~df.isna(axis=1).all()` row mask | `df.dropna(how=\\\"all\\\")`, or build the mask without the `isna(axis=...)` kwarg. |\\n| chained assignment `df[a][b] = x` | `df.loc[row, col] = x` (Copy-on-Write errors on chained sets). |\\n| `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` (ruff UP017) | `datetime.now(UTC)`; `from datetime import UTC`. |\\n| mypy chokes: `object` has no `.loc/.columns` | after `isinstance(data, pd.DataFrame)` guard, rebind to a named `pd.DataFrame` local (or cast) before using the pandas API. |\\n- `pd.to_datetime(x, errors=\\\"coerce\\\")` + `.dt.date` still work; `pd.to_numeric(series, errors=\\\"coerce\\\")` is the null-tolerant close coercion.\\n- LakeStore returns `date` as a datelike column (`datetime64[us]`) on read even though writes accept plain `date` — assert on `set(raw[\\\"ticker\\\"])` and `adj_close`, not raw equality of the date column.\\n\\n## Typing under mypy strict (this venv)\\n- `cast(LakeStore, x)` where the class is imported only under `TYPE_CHECKING` raises `NameError` at runtime — use the string form `cast(\\\"LakeStore\\\", x)` (mypy resolves it, no runtime name lookup).\\n- Heavy deps stay import-free at runtime: `if TYPE_CHECKING: from spx_momentum.data.store import LakeStore`, public signature keeps `store: object`, cast at the call site. This is the established scaffold pattern — keep it.\\n\\n## uv (venv has no pip/ensurepip)\\n- `export PATH=\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\\\"` then `uv add \\\"pkg>=ver\\\"` (also re-syncs env; `import spx_momentum` then works without `PATH=src`).\\n- If uv missing: `curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh`, then confirm `~/.local/bin/uv`.\\n- Run tools via `.venv/bin/python|pytest|ruff|mypy`, never bare system `python3`.\\n\\n## Gate order (repo root)\\n```bash\\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_<mod>.py -v\\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q\\n.venv/bin/ruff check .\\n.venv/bin/mypy src      # strict; ignore pyright/editor pandas-stub noise\\n```\\n\", \"file_type\": \".md\", \"_source_path\": \"/home/ttran/.hermes/skills/software-development/spx-momentum-task-execution/references/fetching-and-pandas3.md\"}", "tool_call_id": "call_602psigb", "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": "skill_view", "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791474367.7282887, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "0a1276bc756f4e5f9023ccb407620087", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": "9f5c067ea7e444058d93e3b779986ccf"}, {"id": 956, "session_id": "20261008_104421_77970a", "role": "tool", "content": "{\"total_count\": 1, \"matches\": [{\"path\": \"/home/ttran/code/trading_data_platform/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-05-spx-momentum-scaffold.md\", \"line\": 369, \"content\": \"## Task 8: Strategy base + signal (`strategy/`)\"}]}", "tool_call_id": "call