as `pd.Series(dtype=float)` (empty). So on the first day, `w_new.sub(w_prev, fill_value=0)` = w_new - 0 = w_new (with missing tickers filled to 0). Then turnover = 0.5 * sum(|w_new|). For fully-invested, that's 0.5.\n\nThis matches my algorithm. Good.\n\nLet me now also think about whether I should sort positions.dates or assume they're already sorted. The strategy (Task 8) returns sorted dates, but for robustness I should sort them here. Let me use `sorted(positions.dates)`.\n\nOK let me actually write the code now. I'll keep it clean and well-documented.\n\nOne last consideration: the trade_log. The plan says columns (date, ticker, weight_before, weight_after, cost). I'll use these column names exactly.\n\nLet me write it.", "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "f721c20a62d745ba8bda4e6d369e35a4", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": "{\"call_919dcl82\": \"5601eedd88124edaa53ccd4d5fe9ce0b\", \"call_a89ncd1x\": \"4fbcecd865ab4a15865eddd347ac2988\"}", "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 1063, "session_id": "20261008_104421_77970a", "role": "tool", "content": "{\"bytes_written\": 6719, \"dirs_created\": true, \"verified\": true, \"lint\": {\"status\": \"ok\", \"output\": \"\"}, \"lsp_diagnostics\": \"LSP diagnostics introduced by this edit:\\n<diagnostics file=\\\"/home/ttran/code/trading_data_platform/src/spx_momentum/backtest/engine.py\\\">\\nERROR [131:25] Argument of type \\\"Timestamp | NaTType\\\" cannot be assigned to parameter \\\"object\\\" of type \\\"Timestamp\\\" in function \\\"append\\\" Type \\\"Timestamp | NaTType\\\" is not assignable to type \\\"Timestamp\\\" \\\"NaTType\\\" is not assignable to \\\"Timestamp\\\" [reportArgumentType] (Pyright)\\nERROR [138:25] Argument of type \\\"Self@Series | Unknown | Any | Series | ndarray[_AnyShape, dt