ustom backtester, report + dashboard, and a network-free test harness — so that\\n12|every module exists, has a typed interface, and imports cleanly.\\n13|\\n14|**Architecture:** A single Python package `spx_momentum` with file-based task passing\\n15|(every stage reads/writes Parquet in a lake layout, no in-memory handoff), wrapped by one\\n16|thin Airflow DAG. A hand-written pandas/numpy backtester sits downstream of the strategy.\\n17|Streamlit reads the artifacts.\\n18|\\n19|**Tech Stack:** Python 3.12 (uv, pinned via `.python-version`), pandas/numpy, DuckDB +\\n20|Parquet, Pydantic, yfinance, Airflow (Docker Compose / `airflow standalone`), Streamlit,\\n21|matplotlib, pytest, ruff, mypy, pre-commit.\\n22|\\n23|**Spec:** `DESIGN-DOC.md` (repo root). This plan scaffolds §4 (architecture + repo layout),\\n24|§4.4 (idempotency), and §4.5 (test strategy skeleton).\\n25|\\n26|## Global Constraints (copied verbatim from the spec)\\n27|\\n28|- Python **3.12** pinned (`.python-version`); no reliance on system Python 3.14 wheels.\\n29|- Strategy: cross-sectional momentum, **top-N monthly rotation, N default 20**, lookback\\n30|  **12 months skip 1** (classic 12-1). Rebalance on **last trading day of month**.\\n31|- Data store: **DuckDB over Parquet** in a lake layout: `data/` → `raw/`, `clean/`,\\n32|  `features/`, `positions/`, `results/`.\\n33|- Transaction cost bps + slippage bps are **configurable**, applied one-way on turnover.\\n34|- **No network in tests** (yfinance monkeypatched; universe is a fixture).\\n35|- Daily bars only; no intraday. No live/paper trading; no broker integrations.\\n36|- Package is framework-agnostic: task functions in `src/spx_momentum/pipeline/tasks.py`\\n37|  have **no Airflow imports** and pass explicit file paths (file-based I/O).\\n38|- Each stage writes to its own lake dir keyed by **(ticker, date)** with **upsert** semantics\\n39|  → idempotent, safe reruns.\\n40|\\n41|## Review Focus (failure modes the spec implies but a scaffold won't yet exercise)\\n42|\\n43|- **A single dead ticker must never fail the DAG** → ingest isolates per-ticker; scaffold\\n44|  the `FetchManifest` type now so the isolation contract is visible.\\n45|- **Transform must fail loudly (not propagate bad data)** → a failed validation gate raises;\\n46|  scaffold `ValidationGateError` + the gate signature.\\n47|- **Top-N selection picks the actual top performers** → the invariant test owns this; scaffold\\n48|  the `PositionSet` shape so the test can assert it.\\n49|- **No-cost equity curve must equal the hand-computed geometric product** → scaffold the\\n50|  `BacktestResult` + `run_backtest` signature so the exact-match test has a target.\\n51|- **Rebalance only on schedule dates; weights sum to 1 before costs** → scaffold\\n52|  `generate_positions` + `Strategy.generate_target_weights` signatures.\\n53|\\n54|---\\n55|\\n56|## File Structure (decomposition locked here)\\n57|\\n58|```\\n59|trading_data_platform/                       # == repo root (a.k.a. spx-momentum/)\\n60|  pyproject.toml            # uv-managed; deps + ruff/mypy/pytest config inline\\n61|  .python-version           # 3.12\\n62|  .gitignore                # data/, artifacts/, .venv/, __pycache__\\n63|  README.md                 # how to sync/test/run-dag/dashboard\\n64|  Makefile                  # sync, test, lint, run-dag, dashboard\\n65|  docker-compose.yaml       # airflow webserver + scheduler + (worker)\\n66|  dags/\\n67|    momentum_dag.py         # THIN: imports package task fns, wires deps + retries\\n68|  config/\\n69|    default.yaml            # cfg defaults (N, lookback, cost/slip bps, paths)\\n70|  data/                     # gitignored lake (created at runtime)\\n71|  src/spx_momentum/\\n72|    __init__.py\\n73|    config.py               # Pydantic settings <- config/default.yaml (env-overridable)\\n74|    data/\\n75|      __init__.py\\n76|      store.py              # LakeStore: DuckDB/Parquet upsert + read + sql\\n77|      universe.py           # fetch / validate / snapshot\\n78|      ingest.py             # chunked yfinance + per-ticker retry + manifest\\n79|      transform.py          # validate gate + align calendar + upsert clean\\n80|    features/\\n81|      __init__.py\\n82|      momentum.py           # rolling returns + cross-sectional rank\\n83|    strategy/\\n84|      __init__.py\\n85|      base.py               # Strategy ABC\\n86|      signal.py             # top-N, equal weight, schedule-gated\\n87|    backtest/\\n88|      __init__.py\\n89|      costs.py              # proportional bps + slippage\\n90|      engine.py             # turn over, hold, mark-to-market\\n91|      metrics.py            # CAGR/Sharpe/Sortino/MaxDD/Calmar/turnover/winrate\\n92|      report.py             # report.md + plots -> artifacts/\\n93|    pipeline/\\n94|      __init__.py\\n95|      tasks.py              # task_* fns: explicit typed path I/O, no Airflow\\n96|    ui/\\n97|      __init__.py\\n98|      dashboard.py          # Streamlit app\\n99|  tests/\\n100|    __init__.py\\n101|    conftest.py             # synthetic_price_generator() + universe fixture + tmp lake\\n102|    test_universe.py\\n103|    test_ingest.py          # yfinance monkeypatched\\n104|    test_transform.py\\n105|    test_features.py\\n106|    test_strategy.py\\n107|    test_backtest_engine.py\\n108|    test_backtest_costs.py\\n109|    test_metrics.py\\n110|    test_e2e_smoke.py\\n111|    test_dag_wiring.py\\n112|  docs/\\n113|    methodology.md          # survivorship bias, lookback caveats, cost model\\n114|```\\n115|\\n116|One clear responsibility per file; split by stage/responsibility, not by tech layer. Task\\n117|functions and Airflow wiring are separated (thin DAG, portable tasks). Tests live beside the\\n118|stage they own; `conftest.py` owns the shared synthetic fixture.\\n119|\\n120|---\\n121|\\n122|## Task 1: Repo hygiene + package skeleton\\n123|\\n124|**Files:**\\n125|- Create: `.python-version`, `pyproject.toml`, `.gitignore`, `README.md`, `Makefile`\\n126|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/__init__.py` and the `__init__.py` of every subpackage listed above.\\n127|\\n128|**Interfaces:**\\n129|- Produces: an importable package `spx_momentum` (all subpackages present, empty-but-valid).\\n130|- Pins: `pyproject.toml` `[tool.uv]`-managed deps: `pandas`, `numpy`, `duckdb`, `pydantic`,\\n131|  `pydantic-settings`, `yfinance`, `pyyaml`, `streamlit`, `matplotlib`,\\n132|  `[dev]` `pytest`, `ruff`, `mypy`, `pre-commit`, `apache-airflow`.\\n133|\\n134|**Pseudocode (what \\\"done\\\" looks like):**\\n135|```\\n136|.python-version:               \\\"3.12\\\"\\n137|\\n138|pyproject.toml:                name=\\\"spx-momentum\\\", requires-python=\\\">=3.12,<3.13\\\"\\n139|                               [project.scripts] spx-dashboard = \\\"spx_momentum.ui.dashboard:main\\\"\\n140|                               [tool.ruff] line-length=100, select=[E,F,I,UP,B]\\n141|                               [tool.mypy] python_version=3.12, strict=true\\n142|                               [tool.pytest.ini_options] testpaths=[\\\"tests\\\"]\\n143|\\n144|Makefile:\\n145|  sync    : uv sync\\n146|  test    : uv run pytest\\n147|  lint    : uv run ruff check . && uv run mypy src\\n148|  run-dag : docker compose up airflow  (or: make airflow-standalone)\\n149|  dashboard : uv run streamlit run src/spx_momentum/ui/dashboard.py\\n150|\\n151|__init__.py per subpackage:    empty (or a one-line docstring)\\n152|```\\n153|**Definition of done:** `uv sync` succeeds; `uv run python -c \\\"import spx_momentum\\\"` is clean;\\n154|`uv run ruff check .` and `uv run mypy src` pass on the (empty) skeleton.\\n155|\\n156|---\\n157|\\n158|## Task 2: Config\\n159|\\n160|**Files:**\\n161|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/config.py`, `config/default.yaml`, `tests/test_config.py`\\n162|\\n163|**Interfaces:**\\n164|- Produces: `settings: Settings` (module-level singleton) and\\n165|  `def load_settings(path: str | None = None, **overrides) -> Settings`.\\n166|- Consumes: nothing.\\n167|- `Settings` fields (typed): `universe_source: str`, `top_n: int = 20`,\\n168|  `lookback_months: int = 12`, `skip_months: int = 1`,\\n169|  `rebalance: str = \\\"last_trading_day\\\"`, `cost_bps: float`, `slippage_bps: float`,\\n170|  `data_root: Path`, `artifacts_dir: Path`,\\n171|  `null_ratio_max: float`, `coverage_min: float`,\\n172|  `fetch_chunk_size: int = 25`, `fetch_retries: int = 3`, `fetch_backoff_s: float`.\\n173|\\n174|**Pseudocode:**\\n175|```\\n176|class Settings(pydantic_settings.BaseSettings):\\n177|    top_n: int = 20\\n178|    lookback_months: int = 12\\n179|    skip_months: int = 1\\n180|    cost_bps: float = 5.0\\n181|    slippage_bps: float = 5.0\\n182|    data_root: Path = Path(\\\"data\\\")\\n183|    ...\\n184|def load_settings(path=None, **overrides):\\n185|    base = yaml.safe_load(default_yaml)\\n186|    merged = {**base, **overrides}\\n187|    return Settings(**merged)\\n188|settings = load_settings()\\n189|```\\n190|**Definition of done:** `load_settings()` returns a valid `Settings` from `config/default.yaml`;\\n191|an env var / kwarg override wins; a missing required field raises a typed Pydantic error.\\n192|\\n193|---\\n194|\\n195|## Task 3: Data store (`store.py`)\\n196|\\n197|**Files:**\\n198|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/data/store.py`, `tests/test_store.py`\\n199|\\n200|**Interfaces:**\\n201|- Produces: `class LakeStore`:\\n202|  - `__init__(self, root: Path)`\\n203|  - `write_upsert(df: pd.DataFrame, stage: Stage, key_cols: tuple[str, str]) -> Path`\\n204|  - `read(stage: Stage) -> pd.DataFrame`\\n205|  - `sql(query: str) -> pd.DataFrame`\\n206|  - `close() -> None`\\n207|- Enums: `Stage = Enum{RAW, CLEAN, FEATURES, POSITIONS, RESULTS}`.\\n208|- Consumes: `Settings.data_root`.\\n209|\\n210|**Pseudocode:**\\n211|```\\n212|class LakeStore:\\n213|    def __init__(self, root):        self.root = root; self._conn = duckdb.connect()\\n214|    def write_upsert(self, df, stage, key_cols=(\\\"ticker\\\",\\\"date\\\")):\\n215|        # partition by stage dir; upsert = read existing, merge on key_cols, write back\\n216|        # idempotent: rerunning with same df yields same rows (no dupes)\\n217|    def read(self, stage):           # select * from <stage>.parquet\\n218|    def sql(self, q):                # returns df via duckdb\\n219|```\\n220|**Definition of done:** write-then-read roundtrip is stable; upserting the same frame twice\\n221|leaves row count unchanged; `sql(\\\"select count(*) ...\\\")` works against a written stage.\\n222|\\n223|---\\n224|\\n225|## Task 4: Universe (`universe.py`)\\n226|\\n227|**Files:**\\n228|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/data/universe.py`, `tests/test_universe.py`\\n229|\\n230|**Interfaces:**\\n231|- Produces:\\n232|  - `def fetch_universe(source: str) -> pd.DataFrame`  # columns: ticker (str)\\n233|  - `def validate_universe(df: pd.DataFrame) -> None`  # raises on bad shape\\n234|  - `def snapshot_universe(df: pd.DataFrame, path: Path, fetch_date: date) -> Path`\\n235|- Consumes: `Settings.universe_source`.\\n236|- Contract: `validate_universe` raises `UniverseValidationError` if any ticker is not\\n237|  well-formed (uppercase alnum, `.`/`-` allowed) or if `not (480 <= len(df) <= 530)`.\\n238|\\n239|**Pseudocode:**\\n240|```\\n241|def fetch_universe(source):\\n242|    if source == \\\"wikipedia\\\":        # pin a parsing fn; strict column expectation\\n243|        return parse_wikipedia_spx500(html)   # -> DataFrame[ticker]\\n244|    else:                            # fallback: committed CSV snapshot in git\\n245|        return pd.read_csv(source)[[\\\"ticker\\\"]]\\n246|def validate_universe(df):\\n247|    assert df[\\\"ticker\\\"].notna().all()\\n248|    if not df[\\\"ticker\\\"].str.fullmatch(r\\\"[A-Z]{1,6}[.-]?[A-Z]{0,3}\\\").all(): raise UniverseValidationError\\n249|    if not (480 <= len(df) <= 530):   raise UniverseValidationError\\n250|def snapshot_universe(df, path, fetch_date):\\n251|    df.assign(fetched=fetch_date).to_csv(path)     # committed fallback\\n252|    return path\\n253|```\\n254|**Definition of done:** a well-formed 500-row frame validates; a 501-off-by-one or a lowercase\\n255|ticker raises `UniverseValidationError`; snapshot writes a CSV with a `fetched` column.\\n256|\\n257|---\\n258|\\n259|## Task 5: Ingest (`ingest.py`) — the isolation contract lives here\\n260|\\n261|**Files:**\\n262|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/data/ingest.py`, `tests/test_ingest.py`\\n263|\\n264|**Interfaces:**\\n265|- Produces:\\n266|  - `@dataclass FetchRecord: ticker, ok: bool, rows: int, nulls: int, ts: datetime, error: str|None`\\n267|  - `def ingest(tickers: pd.DataFrame, start: date, end: date, store: LakeStore, cfg: Settings) -> list[FetchRecord]`\\n268|- Consumes: `LakeStore.write_upsert`, `Settings.fetch_*`.\\n269|- Contract: **one failed ticker never raises out of `ingest`**; failures are captured as a\\n270|  `FetchRecord(ok=False)` row. Returns one record per ticker (including failures).\\n271|\\n272|**Pseudocode:**\\n273|```\\n274|def _download_chunk(chunk: list[str], start, end) -> dict[str, px_df]:\\n275|    # yfinance.download(chunk, start, end, auto_adjust=True)  # ~25/call\\n276|    # per-ticker retry: for attempt in range(cfg.fetch_retries):\\n277|    #     try: ... return  except TransientError: sleep(cfg.fetch_backoff_s * 2**attempt)\\n278|def ingest(tickers, start, end, store, cfg):\\n279|    records = []\\n280|    for chunk in chunked(tickers[\\\"ticker\\\"], cfg.fetch_chunk_size):\\n281|        data = _download_chunk(chunk, start, end)\\n282|        for t in chunk:\\n283|            if t in data and data[t].notna().any().any():\\n284|                store.write_upsert(with_ticker(data[t]), Stage.RAW, (\\\"ticker\\\",\\\"date\\\"))\\n285|                records.append(FetchRecord(t, True, len(data[t]), nulls, now, None))\\n286|            else:\\n287|                records.append(FetchRecord(t, False, 0, 0, now, \\\"no data / transient\\\"))\\n288|    return records                      # never raises for a single bad ticker\\n289|```\\n290|**Definition of done:** with yfinance monkeypatched, a batch where ticker #37 returns an\\n291|exception still yields N records, one `ok=False` for #37, and the rest `ok=True`; the raw\\n292|stage contains the good tickers only.\\n293|\\n294|---\\n295|\\n296|## Task 6: Transform (`transform.py`) — the validation gate lives here\\n297|\\n298|**Files:**\\n299|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/data/transform.py`, `tests/test_transform.py`\\n300|\\n301|**Interfaces:**\\n302|- Produces:\\n303|  - `class ValidationGateError(Exception)` carrying `(ticker, metric, value, limit)`\\n304|  - `def transform(raw: pd.DataFrame, store: LakeStore, cfg: Settings) -> pd.DataFrame`\\n305|- Consumes: `Stage.RAW`, `Stage.CLEAN`, `Settings.null_ratio_max`, `Settings.coverage_min`.\\n306|- Contract: uses **adjusted close**; aligns all tickers to a **common trading calendar**\\n307|  (the union/intersection per cfg); upserts clean keyed by (ticker, date); **raises\\n308|  `ValidationGateError`** if any ticker's null-ratio > `null_ratio_max` or date-coverage\\n309|  < `coverage_min` (fails loudly, does not propagate bad rows).\\n310|\\n311|**Pseudocode:**\\n312|```\\n313|def transform(raw, store, cfg):\\n314|    cal = trading_calendar(raw[\\\"date\\\"])                  # common axis\\n315|    for ticker, g in raw.groupby(\\\"ticker\\\"):\\n316|        g = g.set_index(\\\"date\\\").reindex(cal)\\n317|        null_ratio = g[\\\"adj_close\\\"].isna().mean()\\n318|        coverage   = g[\\\"adj_close\\\"].notna().mean()\\n319|        if null_ratio > cfg.null_ratio_max:  raise ValidationGateError(ticker,\\\"null_ratio\\\",null_ratio,cfg.null_ratio_max)\\n320|        if coverage < cfg.coverage_min:      raise ValidationGateError(ticker,\\\"coverage\\\",coverage,cfg.coverage_min)\\n321|        clean = g[[\\\"adj_close\\\"]]                        # + OHLCV if needed\\n322|    store.write_upsert(clean_all, Stage.CLEAN, (\\\"ticker\\\",\\\"date\\\"))\\n323|    return clean_all\\n324|```\\n325|**Definition of done:** a ticker with 40% nulls (limit 20%) makes `transform` raise\\n326|`ValidationGateError` naming the ticker + metric; a clean frame upserts idempotently to CLEAN.\\n327|\\n328|---\\n329|\\n330|## Task 7: Momentum features (`features/momentum.py`)\\n331|\\n332|**Files:**\\n333|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/features/momentum.py`, `tests/test_features.py`\\n334|\\n335|**Interfaces:**\\n336|- Produces:\\n337|  - `def rolling_returns(prices: pd.DataFrame, months=(3,6,12), skip_months=1) -> pd.DataFrame`\\n338|  - `def cross_sectional_scores(ret: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame`  # per date, rank in [0,1]\\n339|  - `def build_features(prices: pd.DataFrame, store: LakeStore, cfg: Settings) -> pd.DataFrame`\\n340|- Consumes: `Stage.CLEAN`, `Stage.FEATURES`.\\n341|- Contract: `skip_months=1` drops the most recent month from each window (classic 12-1);\\n342|  output is per-date score tables, deterministic, pure pandas.\\n343|\\n344|**Pseudocode:**\\n345|```\\n346|def rolling_returns(prices, months=(3,6,12), skip_months=1):\\n347|    out = {}\\n348|    for m in months:\\n349|        end = prices.shift(m*skip_months)            # drop last `skip` month\\n350|        start = prices.shift(m*(1+skip_months))\\n351|        out[f\\\"ret_{m}m\\\"] = end / start - 1\\n352|    return pd.DataFrame(out)\\n353|def cross_sectional_scores(ret):\\n354|    combined = (ret[\\\"ret_12m\\\"].rank(pct=True) * .5 + ret[\\\"ret_6m\\\"].rank(pct=True) * .3\\n355|                + ret[\\\"ret_3m\\\"].rank(pct=True) * .2)\\n356|    return combined                                   # per date, per ticker score\\n357|def build_features(prices, store, cfg):\\n358|    px = prices[[\\\"adj_close\\\"]].unstack()             # index=date, cols=ticker\\n359|    scores = cross_sectional_scores(rolling_returns(px, (3,6,12), cfg.skip_months))\\n360|    store.write_upsert(scores.reset_index().melt(...), Stage.FEATURES, ...)\\n361|    return scores\\n362|```\\n363|**Definition of done:** with a seeded synthetic price frame, `rolling_returns` uses the\\n364|skipped month boundary correctly; scores are a per-date cross-section and are reproducible\\n365|across two runs.\\n366|\\n367|---\\n368|\\n369|## Task 8: Strategy base + signal (`strategy/`)\\n370|\\n371|**Files:**\\n372|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/strategy/base.py`, `src/spx_momentum/strategy/signal.py`,\\n373|  `tests/test_strategy.py`\\n374|\\n375|**Interfaces:**\\n376|- Produces:\\n377|  - `@dataclass PositionSet: dates: list[date], weights: pd.DataFrame`  # index=date, cols=ticker\\n378|  - `class Strategy(abc.ABC)`: `@abstractmethod generate_target_weights(self, prices, features, as_of: date) -> PositionSet`\\n379|  - `class MomentumStrategy(Strategy)`\\n380|  - `def select_top_n(scores_row: pd.Series, n: int) -> list[str]`\\n381|  - `def equal_weights(tickers: list[str]) -> tuple[float]`  # sums to 1.0\\n382|- Consumes: `Settings.top_n`, `Settings.rebalance`.\\n383|- Contract: rebalance **only on schedule dates** (last trading day of month); weights sum to\\n384|  **1.0 before costs**; on non-schedule dates it carries the last PositionSet forward.\\n385|\\n386|**Pseudocode:**\\n387|```\\n388|class Strategy(ABC):\\n389|    @abstractmethod\\n390|    def generate_target_weights(self, prices, features, as_of) -> PositionSet: ...\\n391|def select_top_n(row, n):\\n392|    return row.dropna().nlargest(n).index.tolist()\\n393|def equal_weights(tickers):\\n394|    w = 1.0/len(tickers);  return [w]*len(tickers)\\n395|class MomentumStrategy(Strategy):\\n396|    def __init__(self, cfg): self.cfg = cfg\\n397|    def generate_target_weights(self, prices, features, as_of):\\n398|        sched = months_end(features.index)\\n399|        pos = {}\\n400|        for d in features.index:\\n401|            if d in sched:\\n402|                top = select_top_n(features.loc[d], self.cfg.top_n)\\n403|                pos[d] = equal_weights(top)           # -> 1.0\\n404|            # else: inherit prior pos (no trading)\\n405|        return PositionSet(sorted(pos), pd.DataFrame(pos))\\n406|```\\n407|**Definition of done:** on the synthetic features, selection picks the actual top performers;\\n408|`weights.loc[d].sum() == 1.0` (within float tol) on every schedule date; no PositionSet changes\\n409|on non-schedule dates.\\n410|\\n411|---\\n412|\\n413|## Task 9: Backtest — costs (leaf)\\n414|\\n415|**Files:**\\n416|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/backtest/costs.py`, `tests/test_backtest_costs.py`\\n417|\\n418|**Interfaces:**\\n419|- Produces:\\n420|  - `def apply_costs(notional: float, cost_bps: float, slippage_bps: float) -> float`\\n421|    # returns total cost = notional * (cost_bps + slippage_bps) / 10_000 (one-way, on traded notional)\\n422|- Consumes: `Settings.cost_bps`, `Settings.slippage_bps`.\\n423|\\n424|**Pseudocode:**\\n425|```\\n426|def apply_costs(notional, cost_bps=5.0, slippage_bps=5.0):\\n427|    return notional * (cost_bps + slippage_bps) / 1e4\\n428|```\\n429|**Definition of done:** `apply_costs(1_000_000, 5, 5) == 1_000` exactly (within float tol);\\n430|zero bps → 0.0.\\n431|\\n432|---\\n433|\\n434|## Task 10: Backtest — engine\\n435|\\n436|**Files:**\\n437|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/backtest/engine.py`, `tests/test_backtest_engine.py`\\n438|\\n439|**Interfaces:**\\n440|- Produces:\\n441|  - `@dataclass BacktestResult: equity_curve: pd.Series, trade_log: pd.DataFrame, exposure: pd.Series, terminal_value: float`\\n442|  - `def run_backtest(prices: pd.DataFrame, positions: PositionSet, cfg: Settings) -> BacktestResult`\\n443|- Consumes: `PositionSet`, `Settings` (cost/slip bps), `apply_costs`.\\n444|- Contract: on each **rebalance date** compute `turnover = 0.5*Σ|w_new − w_old|`, apply\\n445|  `apply_costs` to `turnover * current equity`; **hold** weights and **mark-to-market daily**\\n446|  between rebalances. No-cost run's equity must equal the hand-computed geometric product of\\n447|  held returns (exact, within float tol).\\n448|\\n449|**Pseudocode:**\\n450|```\\n451|@dataclass\\n452|class BacktestResult:\\n453|    equity_curve: pd.Series          # indexed by date\\n454|    trade_log:   pd.DataFrame        # (date, ticker, weight_before, weight_after, cost)\\n455|    exposure:    pd.Series\\n456|    terminal_value: float\\n457|def run_backtest(prices, positions, cfg):\\n458|    equity = 1.0\\n459|    curve, trades = [], []\\n460|    w_prev = pd.Series(dtype=float)\\n461|    for d in positions.dates:\\n462|        w_new = positions.weights.loc[d]\\n463|        turnover = 0.5*(w_new.sub(w_prev, fill_value=0)).abs().sum()\\n464|        cost = apply_costs(turnover * equity, cfg.cost_bps, cfg.slippage_bps)\\n465|        equity *= (1 - turnover*(cfg.cost_bps+cfg.slippage_bps)/1e4)   # cost drag\\n466|        equity *= held_return(prices, d, w_new)                         # mark-to-market\\n467|        curve.append((d, equity)); trades.append(log(d, w_prev, w_new, cost))\\n468|        w_prev = w_new\\n469|    return BacktestResult(pd.Series(curkey...), pd.DataFrame(trades), exposure, equity)\\n470|```\\n471|**Definition of done:** a **0 bp** backtest's equity equals `∏ (1 + held_return)` over the\\n472|same held periods (assert equal within 1e-9); adding any bps strictly lowers\\n473|`terminal_value`.\\n474|\\n475|---\\n476|\\n477|## Task 11: Backtest — metrics\\n478|\\n479|**Files:**\\n480|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/backtest/metrics.py`, `tests/test_metrics.py`\\n481|\\n482|**Interfaces:**\\n483|- Produces (all pure, take the `BacktestResult` + optional benchmark):\\n484|  - `def cagr(equity: pd.Series) -> float`\\n485|  - `def annualized_vol(equity: pd.Series) -> float`\\n486|  - `def sharpe(equity: pd.Series, rf=0.0) -> float`\\n487|  - `def sortino(equity: pd.Series, rf=0.0) -> float`\\n488|  - `def max_drawdown(equity: pd.Series) -> tuple[float, date]`  # dd value + date\\n489|  - `def calmar(equity: pd.Series) -> float`\\n490|  - `def total_turnover(trade_log: pd.DataFrame) -> float`\\n491|  - `def regime_win_rate(positions: PositionSet) -> float`      # win rate on rebalances\\n492|  - `def vs_benchmark(equity, benchmark: pd.Series) -> dict`     # excess CAGR, etc.\\n493|- Consumes: `BacktestResult`.\\n494|\\n495|**Pseudocode:**\\n496|```\\n497|cagr        = mean_ret  -> (terminal)**(1/years) - 1\\n498|annualized_vol = std(daily_ret) * sqrt(252)\\n499|sharpe      = mean(daily_ret) / std(daily_ret) * sqrt(252)\\n500|sortino     = mean(daily_ret) / std(downside) * sqrt(252)\\n501|max_drawdown= min(equity/cummax(equity) - 1)  + argmin date\\n502|calmar      = cagr / abs(max_dd)\\n503|```\\n504|**Definition of done:** on a **6-observation toy series** each metric equals a\\n505|closed-form hand calculation (assert exact within 1e-9); `max_drawdown` returns the correct\\n506|date.\\n507|\\n508|---\\n509|\\n510|## Task 12: Backtest — report\\n511|\\n512|**Files:**\\n513|- Create: `src/spx_momentum/backtest/report.py`, (no dedicated unit test — covered by\\n514|  `test_e2e_smoke.py`)\\n515|\\n516|**Interfaces:**\\n517|- Produces: `def write_report(result: BacktestResult, metrics: dict, artifacts_dir: Path) -> Path`\\n518|- Consumes: `BacktestResult`.\\n519|- Writes: `artifacts/report.md` (metrics table + survivorship-bias note from methodology) +\\n520|  `artifacts/equity_curve.png` + `artifacts/drawdown.png` + `artifacts/holdings_heatmap.png`\\n521|  (matplotlib, no JS deps).\\n522|\\n523|**Pseudocode:**\\n524|```\\n525|def write_report(result, metrics, artifacts_dir):\\n526|    artifacts_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n527|    (artifacts_dir/\\\"report.md\\\").write_text(render_md(metrics))\\n528|    plot_equity(result.equity_curve)   -> equity_curve.png\\n529|    plot_drawdown(result.equity_curve)-> drawdown.png\\n530|    plot_holdings(heatmap)            -> holdings_heatmap.png\\n531|    return artifacts_dir/\\\"report.md\\\"\\n532|```\\n533|**Definition of done:** given a `BacktestResult`, `write_report` e