aFrame(px, index=idx)\\n659|@pytest.fixture\\n660|def universe_fixture(): return pd.DataFrame({\\\"ticker\\\":[f\\\"T{i:03d}\\\" for i in range(500)]})\\n661|@pytest.fixture\\n662|def lake(tmp_path):     return LakeStore(tmp_path/\\\"data\\\")\\n663|```\\n664|**Key invariants the stub tests must pin (one assert line each):**\\n665|```\\n666|test_features        : rolling_returns uses skip-month boundary\\n667|test_strategy        : select_top_n picks actual top + weights sum to 1.0\\n668|test_backtest_engine : no-cost equity == Σ geometric product (1e-9)\\n669|test_backtest_costs  : 10bp cost strictly lowers terminal; delta == turnover-weighted\\n670|test_metrics         : 6-obs toy series matches closed-form\\n671|test_e2e_smoke       : full task chain → consistent row counts per stage\\n672|test_dag_wiring      : 7-task chain; only ingest retries=2\\n673|```\\n674|**Definition of done:** `uv run pytest` collects all stubs; every invariant above is expressible\\n675|against the scaffolded interfaces; `docs/methodology.md` documents survivorship bias + 12-1\\n676|lookback + cost model.\\n677|\\n678|---\\n679|\\n680|## Self-Review (run against the spec)\\n681|\\n682|- **Coverage:** §4.2 components → Tasks 2–12; §4.3 layout → File Structure; §4.4 idempotency\\n683|  → Tasks 3/5/6 (upsert + gate); §4.5 test strategy → Task 16 + per-task stubs; §5 risks →\\n684|  ingest isolation (T5), Wikipedia fallback (T4), 3.12 pin (T1), Airflow friction (T14).\\n685|- **Type consistency check:** `PositionSet` (T8) is consumed by `run_backtest` (T10) and\\n686|  `regime_win_rate` (T11) — consistent. `BacktestResult` (T10) is consumed by `metrics`\\n687|  (T11) and `report` (T12) — consistent. `LakeStore.write_upsert(df, Stage, key_cols)`\\n688|  (T3) is used identically in T5/T6/T7 — consistent. `Settings` (T2) fields referenced by\\n689|  later tasks (`top_n`, `skip_months`, `cost_bps`, `null_ratio_max`) all exist in T2. ✓\\n690|- **Proportion:** each task carries only the interface + one pseudocode sketch + a\\n691|  definition of done; no full implementation bodies transcribed. ✓ (per user: pseudocode only)\\n692|\\n693|## Execution note\\n694|\\n695|Per the user's instruction, this stays a **scaffold (pseudocode, not coded)**. When you're ready\\n696|to build it out, each task above maps 1:1 to a code task with a real TDD loop (failing test →\\n697|stub → pass → commit).\", \"total_lines\": 697, \"file_size\": 31549, \"truncated\": false, \"is_binary\": false, \"is_image\": false, \"not_found\": false}", "tool_call_id": "call_xfhquykq", "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": "read_file", "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791379225.3106458, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "c8417b4db91241a2953a6bc4432a314f", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": "e553c2e3c96e43f7b103019372af7580"}, {"id": 293, "session_id": "20261007_081732_0eaadc", "role": "tool", "content": "{\"content\": \"1|# Methodology: how the system works and its biases.\\n2|# DESIGN-DOC §4.3 / §5 — the report and dashboard both cite this file, so the\\n3|# claims below are the single source of truth.\\n4|\\n5|# Methodology — S&P 500 Cross-Sectional Momentum\\n6|\\n7|## What the system does\\n8|\\n9|1. **Universe** — S&P 500 constituents are scraped from Wikipedia (pinned\\n10|   parser, strict validation 480–530 well-formed tickers) and date-stamped\\n11|   into a CSV snapshot. A committed CSV in git is the fallback if the scrape\\n12|   format changes.\\n13|2. **Ingest** — daily OHLCV from Yahoo Finance (yfinance, adjusted close),\\n14|   chunked (~25 tickers/call), per-ticker retry (3x, exponential backoff).\\n15|   One failing ticker never fails the run; it lands in a fetch-manifest table.\\n16|3. **Transform** — null-ratio and date-coverage gates per ticker; on breach\\n17|   the stage fails loudly. All tickers are aligned to a common trading\\n18|   calendar. Output is upserted (key: ticker, date) — reruns are idempotent.\\n19|4. **Features** — rolling 3/6/12-month returns (skipping the most recent 1\\n20|   month: the classic 12-1 signal) blended into a per-date cross-sectional\\n21|   score.\\n22|5. **Signal** — on the last trading day of each month, hold the top N=20 by\\n23|   score, equal-weighted; weights sum to 1 before costs; otherwise carry\\n24|   forward.\\n25|6. **Backtest** — custom engine (no library): turnover computed as\\n26|   `0.5 * sum |Δw|` on each rebalance, cost + slippage applied one-way on\\n27|   traded notional, mark-to-market daily, equity curve + trade log.\\n28|7. **Report** — CAGR, annualized vol, Sharpe, Sortino, max drawdown (+date),\\n29|   Calmar, turnover, win-rate, vs equal-weight S&P 500 benchmark. Artifacts\\n30|   are deterministic (same inputs → same outputs).\\n31|\\n32|## Known biases and caveats (honest reporting)\\n33|\\n34|- **Survivorship bias** — the constituent list is *today's* S&P 500. Tickers\\n35|  that were delisted, merged, or dropped during the backtest window are not\\n36|  in the universe, and back-in would flatter returns. This is a material\\n37|  upward bias for long-horizon backtests; see DESIGN-DOC §5 for the mitigation\\n38|  (committed snapshot as the best available proxy).\\n39|- **Lookback window & 1-month skip** — the 12-1 convention avoids the well\\n40|  documented short-term reversal that contaminates raw 12-month momentum.\\n41|- **Costs are a simplification** — bps applied to traded notional only.\\n42|  Market impact for very large notional, queue effects at rebalance time and\\n43|  borrow/dividend frictions are NOT modeled.\\n44|- **Benchmark** — equal-weight SPY as proxy; actual index (cap-weighted) is\\n45|  strictly better for a fair comparison but we use EW for a clean \\\"does the\\n46|  signal add\\\" read.\\n47|- **No live trading** — this is a research tool. Nothing places, simulates,\\n48|  or routes real orders (DESIGN-DOC §1 non-goal).\\n49|\\n50|## Reproducibility\\n51|\\n52|- All inputs (synthetic fixtures or committed YAML + committed universe CSV)\\n53|  are pinned. Running the full chain twice gives bit-identical artifacts\\n54|  (float-tol 1e-9). Any non-determinism (e.g. yfinance returning a different\\n55|  row count) is a *data* issue, flagged by the null-ratio / coverage gates.\", \"total_lines\": 55, \"file_size\": 3095, \"truncated\": false, \"is_binary\": false, \"is_image\": false, \"not_found\": false}", "tool_call_id": "call_s92f05sb", "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": "read_file", "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791379225.3190176, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "906c9c08a1f84a1db4e3497985c81fbf", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": "904887808fdf432a9ac6c4206770dde7"}, {"id": 294, "session_id": "20261007_081732_0eaadc", "role": "assistant", "content": "I'll check the existing files to see what's already scaffolded and what's still stubbed.", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_j0f9s5s2", "call_id": "call_j0f9s5s2", "response_item_id": "fc_j0f9s5s2", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "read_file", "arguments": "{\"path\":\"/home/ttran/code/trading_data_platform/DESIGN-DOC.md\"}"}}, {"id": "call_oh1be8qx", "call_id": "call_oh1be8qx", "response_item_id": "fc_oh1be8qx", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "execute_code", "arguments": "{\"code\":\"from hermes_tools import read_file, terminal\\nimport json\