oning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "baca2a14154b4734a9955c5b090418db", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 221, "session_id": "20261006_102945_ece204", "role": "assistant", "content": "## Design — Section 1: Architecture & Components\n\n```\n+--------------------------------------------------------------+\n|  api container (FastAPI)                                     |\n|                                                              |\n|  main.py            config.py         job_store.py           |\n|  (app, routes,      (load+validate    (in-memory JobStore,   |\n|   lifecycle)         yaml config,       status, result,      |\n|                      Pydantic models)  expiry/TTL, lock-free |\n|                                                   access)    |\n|  pipeline.py        llm_client.py     frames.py              |\n|  (orchestrates:     (thin Ollama/OpenAI-  (ffmpeg/opencv      |\n|   validate path →   compatible) chat      frame extraction,   |\n|   extract frames →  wrapper. Both models  cleanup)           |\n|   video LLM →       go through this)                       |\n|   summarize →\n|   validate JSON)\n+--------------------------------------------------------------+\n            |                              ^\n            |  POST /api/jobs              |  frames dir\n            v                              |\n   +----------------+    http    +-------------------+\n   |  caller        |----------->|  Ollama (external) |\n   |  (your client) |            |  :11434            |\n   +----------------+            |  minicpm-v4.5:8b    |\n                                |  + summary model    |\n                                +-------------------+\n```\n\n**Components:**\n\n- **`config.py`** — loads config from a file path given by env `APP_CONFIG` (default `/config.yaml` at container level, `config.yaml` locally). Pydantic models validate shape on startup — a bad config fails the container loudly at boot, never mid-request. No magic defaults in code: every value (model names, base URL, fps, temps, timeouts, path prefixes, schema fields) comes from this file; code may only hold structural defaults like \"port 8080\".\n- **`llm_client.py`** — one `chat(model, messages, **opts)` function. Works against Ollama's OpenAI-compatible endpoint (`{base_url}/v1/chat/completions`) — one client for both models. Retries with backoff on 5xx/timeouts (counts configurable).\n- **`frames.py`** — extracts frames at configured fps to a per-job temp dir; cleanup guaranteed in a `finally` / context manager so failed jobs don't litter disk. Implementation choice (decided during build): `ffmpeg` via subprocess vs `opencv-python` — both work in a slim Docker image; ffmpeg is more robust across codecs.\n- **`pipeline.py`** — the state machine for a job: `queued → extracting → analyzing → summarizing → completed | failed`. Each transition updates the store. Takes no globals; config and client injected (testable).\n- **`job_store.py`** — dict + `threading.Lock`, keyed by `uuid4`. Stores: status, timestamps, current stage, error, result JSON. Jobs older than a configurable TTL are reaped lazily on read.\n- **`main.py`** — FastAPI app, routes, startup = load config + build clients + health endpoint.\n\n**Concurrency model:** a bounded worker pool (size = configured max parallel jobs, default 1 — GPU-bound anyway) pulls from an in-process queue. Backpressure is real: queue length capped, `POST` returns `429` when full. Jobs are never silently dropped.\n\n**Data flow for one request:**\n\n```\nPOST /api/jobs {\"path\": \"/data/videos/clip.mp4\"}\n  → validate: exists? extension allowed? prefix rewrite from config\n  → create job id, enqueue → 202 {\"job_id\": \"...\", \"status_url\": \"...\"}\n  ... worker: extract frames → video-LLM → validate JSON → summary-LLM → schema-check\n  → GET /api/jobs/{id} → 200 {\"status\":\"completed\", \"result\":{title,summary,actions,subjects,confidence_note}}\n```\n\nDoes this architecture look right before I get into the API contract and config schema details?", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": null, "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791302038.272698, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "reasoning": "The user approved approach A. Now I'll walk through the design section by section, seeking their confirmation after each one.", "reasoning_content": "The user approved approach A. Now I'll walk through the design section by section, seeking their confirmation after each one.", "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "6833f77e0f904d7c98252d240757f8e1", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 222, "session_id": "20261006_102945_ece204", "role": "user", "content": "it looks right", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": null, "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791302089.2860575, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "a42891c13f8449bdb773be3b39fd74fd", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 223, "session_id": "20261006_102945_ece204", "role": "assistant", "content": "## Design — Section 2: API Contract\n\n**Endpoints** (all JSON):\n\n`POST /api/jobs`\n```\nRequest:  {\"path\": \"/data/videos/clip.mp4\"}\nHeaders:  optional Idempotency-Key (re-POSTing the same key within a window\n          returns the original job instead of queueing a duplicate)\n\n202 Accepted  → {\"job_id\": \"3f9c...\", \"status\": \"queued\",\n                   \"status_url\": \"/api/jobs/3f9c...\", \"created_at\": \"...\"}\n\n400           → {\"error\": {\"code\": \"invalid_request\", \"message\": \"...\",\n                            \"details\": {\"field\": \"path\", ...}}}\n404           → code \"path_not_found\" (after prefix rewrite, file doesn't exist)\n415           → code \"unsupported_format\" (not .mp4/.mov/.avi, per config)\n422           → validation error (bad shape) — FastAPI standard\n429           → code \"queue_full\", header Retry-After: <seconds>\n503           → code \"llm_unavailable\" (Ollama unreachable at submit-\n                validation time — actually we lazy-check; this fires on\n                completion, not submit)\n```\n\n**Path rules:** the config declares `path_prefix: {\"host\": \"/data/videos\", \"container\": \"/srv/videos\"}`. The API accepts the **host** path; it must live *under* the host prefix (a path outside it → `400 path_outside_allowed_root`). It's rewritten to the container path before the worker touches it. This both answers \"where do videos live\" and acts as an allow-list (defense in depth: the API can only ever open files under that root).\n\n`GET /api/jobs/{job_id}`\n```\n200  → {\"job_id\", \"status\",\n        \"status\" ∈ queued|extracting|analyzing|summarizing|completed|failed,\n        \"created_at\", \"started_at\"? , \"finished_at\"?,\n        \"result\"?: {\"title\",\"summary\",\"actions\":[...],\"subjects\":[...],\"confidence_note\"},\n        \"error\"?: {\"code\",\"message\"} }\n\n404  → unknown or expired job (code \"job_not_found\")\n```\n\n**Response envelope convention:** success = data at top level (no wrapper); errors = `{\"error\": {\"code\",\"message\",\"details\"?}}` with stable machine-readable `code` strings. Callers branch on `status`/`error.code`, not on message text.\n\n`GET /healthz` → `200 {\"status\":\"ok\"}` (liveness, cheap — no LLM call)\n`GET /readyz` → probes Ollama (`/api/tags` or `/v1/models`); `200` when a model responds, `503` otherwise. Good for Docker `HEALTHCHECK` and for you to debug \"is Ollama up?\" without docker exec.\n\n**Job lifecycle on completion:**\n- `completed` carries `result` (always the validated 5-field object).\n- `failed` carries `error.code` from a closed set: `no_frames`, `video_llm_error`, `video_llm_invalid_output`, `summary_llm_error`, `summary_invalid_output`, `internal_error`. `video_llm_invalid_output` / `summary_invalid_output` means the model returned non-JSON — the pipeline retries N times (configurable) before declaring failure, to ride out flaky structured output.\n- Jobs persist for `job_ttl_seconds` (default 24h) after finishing, then are reaped — after that they 404. Memory stays bounded no matter how many jobs you fire.\n\nOne deliberate omission: **no streaming/SSE**. You chose structured JSON out; long-polling the status URL is the contract. (If polling feels chatty later, an SSE endpoint is a small add-on that reuses the same store — but not now, YAGNI.)\n\nContract OK, or do you want any endpoint/field changed before I write the config schema section?", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": null, "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791302146.7490208, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "reasoning": "Section 2: API Contract.", "reasoning_content": "Section 2: API Contract.", "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "b1fb3b4e41b54641b274f5f858fab3e6", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 224, "session_id": "20261006_102945_ece204", "role": "user", "content": "Contract OK", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": null, "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791302339.739808, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "6720f1cbfbe64d45b9eeefe1aceed024", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 225, "session_id": "20261006_102945_ece204", "role": "assistant", "content": "## Design — Section 3: Config Schema\n\nSource of truth is a single YAML file (JSON also accepted — Pydantic reads both). Path via env `APP_CONFIG`, default `config.yaml` relative to working dir (Docker sets it to the mounted path). **Every** behavior-driving value lives here; the code holds only structural things.\n\n```yaml\nserver:\n  host: \"0.0.0.0\"          # FastAPI/Uvicorn bind\n  port: 8080\n  max_queue_size: 16       # 429 when full\n  max_parallel_jobs: 1     # worker pool size (GPU-bound: keep at 1)\n\npaths:\n  host_prefix: \"/data/videos\"          # what callers send\n  container_prefix: \"/srv/videos\"      # what the API opens\n  allowed_extensions: [\".mp4\", \".mov\", \".avi\"]\n  max_file_size_mb: 2048               # reject absurd inputs early\n\njobs:\n  ttl_seconds: 86400                   # reap after completion\n  idempotency_window_seconds: 600\n\nframes:\n  fps_sample_rate: 1                   # from your sample code\n  max_frames: 900                      # safety cap (3 fps * 5 min video)\n                                       # if exceeded: sample down uniformly,\n                                       # don't fail\n  frame_format: \"jpg\"                  # jpg keeps token counts sane vs png\n\nmodels:\n  base_url: \"http://host.docker.internal:11434\"   # or a LAN IP\n  video_model: \"minicpm-v4.5:8b\"\n  summary_model: \"llama3.1:8b\"         # placeholder — pick your text model\n\nllm:\n  timeout_seconds: 300\n  max_retries: 2                       # on transient failures (5xx/timeout)\n  retry_backoff_seconds: 3             # exponential base\n  temperature_video: 0.5               # matches your sample\n  temperature_summary: 0.2             # lower: structured output wants less\n  max_tokens_video: 4096\n  max_tokens_summary: 1500\n\nprompting:\n  video_system: \"You watch video clips as a sequence of frames...\\nReturn JSON only.\"\n  video_user_suffix: \" This is a video clip. Describe the actions in chronological order.\\nRespond ONLY with JSON matching the schema.\"\n  summary_system: \"You summarize video descriptions. Return JSON only.\"\n  summary_user: \"Given the video description below, produce the final JSON.\\n{description}\"\n\noutput_schema:                        # mirrors the API contract fields\n  fields:\n    title: {type: \"string\", max_length: 120}\n    summary: {type: \"string\", max_length: 600}\n    actions: {type: \"array\", item: \"string\", max_items: 25}\n    subjects: {type: \"array\", item: \"string\", max_items: 20}\n    confidence_note: {type: \"string\", max_length: 200, optional: true}\n\nlogging:\n  level: \"INFO\"                       # DEBUG to trace LLM requests\n  format: \"json\"                      # machine-parseable from docker logs\n```\n\n**Rules the code enforces (startup failure, not runtime surprises):**\n\n- `host_prefix` and `container_prefix` are required; both must be absolute paths.\n- Model names non-empty; `base_url` must be a valid http(s) URL.\n- `max_frames` > 0, `fps_sample_rate` > 0, `ttl_seconds` > 0, `max_parallel_jobs` ≥ 1, `max_queue_size` ≥ 1.\n- `output_schema.fields` — if you later delete `confidence_note`, the pipeline's validator and the prompts are generated from *the same* list, so API contract and prompts can't drift apart. This is the one place I push config-driven code generation: the 5 fields in your answer to Q6 are data, not code.\n\n**Secrets:** no API keys needed (Ollama, local). If you ever switch `base_url` to a hosted provider, `llm.api_key` reads from env `LLM_API_KEY` via a `${LLM_API_KEY}` interpolation in the YAML — so keys *never* live in the config file or the image. (Supported from day one, unused today.)\n\n**`config.yaml.example`** ships in the repo with sensible values; the real `config.yaml` is gitignored. Config is mounted read-only into the container.\n\nOne decision I made for you (flag if you disagree): **`confidence_note` is the only optional field** — the other four must always be present in the summary response, and the validator rejects the summary LLM's output if it omits a required one (triggers the retry-then-fail path). \n\nConfig schema good to go? Next section is error handling & testing strategy.", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": null, "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791302409.6387923, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "reasoning": "Alright, Section 3: the configuration schema. Let's write the YAML design.", "reasoning_content": "Alright, Section 3: the configuration schema. Let's write the YAML design.", "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "fe02df5365994a828bb8bc70de4664bc", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 226, "session_id": "20261006_102945_ece204", "role": "user", "content": "continue", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": null, "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791302554.0957596, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "5b8c7433d344456f99346aa7edb55e76", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 227, "session_id": "20261006_102945_ece204", "role": "assistant", "content": "## Design — Section 4: Error Handling & Testing\n\n**Error-handling policy:**\n\n- **Fail loud at boundaries, fail contained inside a job.** A bad config or an unregistered path prefix = startup failure or clean 400. A mid-job failure (Ollama 500s, frames extraction dies, JSON malformed) = that one job goes to `failed` with a code from the closed set; the API keeps serving, the queue keeps draining, other jobs are unaffected.\n- **No partial results.** A job is `completed` with a full validated result, or `failed`. There's no \"summary came back but subjects were missing\" — the validator is all-or-nothing, and `failed` jobs never leak a half-parsed dict.\n- **Retries are typed:** transient (timeout, 5xx, connection reset) → up to `max_retries` exponential backoffs, then fail with the specific code. Structural (model returns non-JSON) → the retry budget is the *same* retry count but against a re-prompt (the user message gains a \"Your last reply was not valid JSON. Respond only with JSON matching the schema.\" append) — one cheap trick that fixes the common case. Deterministic failures (file not found, bad extension) fail *immediately at submit*, before a job ID is even created → 400/415, not a job that fails one second later. This saves callers from the \"created job → status failed instantly\" dance on their own typos.\n- **Cleanup is contractual:** frame temp dirs and per-job scratch live under an explicit `scratch_root` (configurable, `/tmp/video_processing` by default), removed in the pipeline's `finally` regardless of failure path. A crash leaves orphans; a `startup` hook sweeps `scratch_root` on boot (safe only because *every* scratch path is namespaced by job ID — never touch anything we didn't create).\n- **Timeouts are layered:** per-LLM-call timeout (300s in example) < job-level soft budget (`jobs.max_runtime_seconds`, default 900, enforced by the worker wrapping the pipeline) < nothing else. A job that hits its budget gets `failed: timeout` and its frames are cleaned up — one stuck 20-minute decode can't hold the slot forever.\n- **Log format:** JSON lines. Every log line carries `job_id` when in-job context exists, plus `stage`. Docker logs become directly greppable: `docker logs api | jq 'select(.job_id==\"...\")'`.\n\n**Testing strategy (this is a real gate in the build, not an afterthought):**\n\n- **Unit (fast, no network, no models):**\n  - `config.py`: valid yaml → typed object; each invalid variant (missing prefix, bad port, negative fps, relative path) → startup error. Table-driven, one assertion per rule.\n  - `frames.py`: given a real small test mp4 (generated once by ffmpeg in a fixture, committed as a binary test asset ~50KB), frames come out at the right count/format; bad codec → clear error; `max_frames` cap samples down, not fails.\n  - `llm_client.py`: against `respx`/`httpx` mock — retries on 500, no retry on 400, backoff timing honored, timeout surfaced correctly.\n  - `pipeline.py`: the core suite. Fake LLM client returns (a) valid JSON → `completed` with result; (b) non-JSON then JSON → completes after one re-prompt; (c) always non-JSON → `failed: summary_invalid_output`; (d) video model raises → `failed: video_llm_error`; (e) no frames file → `failed: no_frames` *and* the scratch dir is gone afterwards.\n  - `job_store.py`: status transitions, TTL reaping, idempotency window dedup, queue-full signal.\n- **Integration (one, end-to-end, in Docker):** a `testcontainers`-style compose test — or simpler, just `docker compose up` in CI — POSTs a real small mp4 against a **stubbed Ollama** (a tiny FastAPI stub that returns canned `chat/completions` bodies). Asserts the full path: 202 → poll → completed → exact 5-field schema. This is the single test that proves \"the thing I'm shipping actually behaves.\"\n- **What we deliberately don't test:** the specific video model's output quality (that's a product decision, not a code bug), and load testing beyond the queue-full behavior (covered by unit test).\n\n**One explicit non-goal** (YAGNI): no persistent job database. In-process store, documented as such in the README and in the failure modes list (\"restarts lose in-flight jobs — this is by design for v1; the upgrade path to a broker-backed queue is isolated to `job_store.py`\"). If you ever need durability, that's the swap point, not a rewrite.\n\nError handling & testing OK? That's the last design section before I write the spec doc.", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": null, "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791302625.2394226, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "reasoning": "Continuing work on section 4: Error handling and testing strategy. Let's write a concise, useful section that aligns with what I designed.", "reasoning_content": "Continuing work on section 4: Error handling and testing strategy. Let's write a concise, useful section that aligns with what I designed.", "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "4d4b8849fb824400ab55898bf70c3df8", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 228, "session_id": "20261006_102945_ece204", "role": "user", "content": "continue", "tool_call_id": null, "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": null, "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1791302676.940863, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_c